Consider the Einstein–Vlasov–Maxwell system on a 4-dimensional Lorentzian manifold (M, g), describing a collisionless ensemble of identical particles of rest mass m > 0 and electric charge q ∈ ℝ that interact through both gravity and the electromagnetic field. The unknowns are:

(i) a Lorentzian metric g of signature (−,+,+,+) on M;
(ii) an electromagnetic 2-form F on M with sourced Maxwell equations dF = 0 and ∇^μ F_{μν} = 4π J_ν;
(iii) a nonnegative distribution function f on the mass shell P_m = {(x,p) ∈ TM : g_x(p,p) = −m², p future-directed},

coupled through:
• the Einstein equations R_{μν} − ½ R g_{μν} = 8π (T^{V}_{μν} + T^{EM}_{μν}), where T^{V}_{μν}(x) = ∫_{P_m(x)} f(x,p) p_μ p_ν dvol_{P_m(x)}(p) and T^{EM}_{μν} = (1/4π)(F_{μα} F_ν^{\;α} − ¼ g_{μν} F_{αβ} F^{αβ});
• the charged-particle Vlasov equation along the Lorentz–geodesic flow: p^μ ∂_{x^μ} f + (−Γ^i_{μν} p^μ p^ν + q F^i_{\;μ} p^μ) ∂_{p^i} f = 0;
• the current J^μ(x) = q ∫_{P_m(x)} f(x,p) p^μ dvol_{P_m(x)}(p).

Assume the spacetime admits two commuting Killing vector fields, a timelike ξ and an axial η, generating a stationary and axially symmetric isometry group, with the standard asymptotic flatness conditions at spatial infinity, and that F is invariant under both Killing fields.

Problem. Develop a framework (analytic, numerical, or a combination) that produces stationary, axially symmetric, asymptotically flat solutions (g, F, f) of the above Einstein–Vlasov–Maxwell system with f compactly supported on the mass shell, without restricting to a perturbative regime: that is, allow the total ADM angular momentum J and a measure of gravitational-field strength (e.g., the central redshift or 2M/R ratio) to range over an unrestricted regime, rather than being constrained to a small neighborhood of a known background (such as Minkowski space or a spherically symmetric solution). Establish existence of such solutions and describe their parameter space, including the admissible range of total charge Q, total angular momentum J, and gravitational compactness.

